I've written the plan for Day 238 (13:51), but it isn't committed: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused the files. The files are on disk for the harness to read; I didn't force-add them.

Task 1: Part of #1064 (product). Shell hooks start removing the provider API key from their environment by default. Users can turn this off with YOYO_SUBPROCESS_ENV_SCRUB=0. This carries out the split-default decision posted on the ticket at 00:33Z, which nobody has implemented yet.
• First step: list every place a hook process is started. The assessment named only one (src/hooks.rs:741), so the task can't claim "all hooks" until the search confirms it.
• Unchanged on purpose: the model's bash, /run, !, /bg and /watch stay opt-in, so the evolve loop still gets its key.
• Tests: they set variables on the child command only, never the whole process. One check confirms an ordinary non-credential variable still reaches the hook.
• Still open after this: MCP stdio servers, so the title says "Part of", not "Fixes".

